lesson: 126
title: More by, fewer by
level: primary-1
stars: 1
explain: «7 more than» means add: 7 more than 20 is 20 + 7 = 27.
explain: Read carefully who has more. «Ann has 20, that is 7 fewer than Ben» means Ben has more: Ben has 20 + 7 = 27.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing n=3..50 k=2..30
need: n + k <= 80
answer: n + k
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {b} has {k} more {t} than {a}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} has {k} fewer {t} than {b}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: There are {n} {t} on the shelf and {k} more on the table than on the shelf. How many {t} are on the table?
exercise: {a} made {n} jumps with the rope. {b} made {k} more jumps than {a}. How many jumps did {b} make?
exercise: Which number is {k} more than {n}?
test: {b} has some {t}. {a} has {n}, which is {k} fewer than {b}. How many {t} does {b} have?
test: {k} less than a number is {n}. What is the number?
test: {a} collected {n} {t}. {b} collected {k} more {t} than {a}. How many {t} did {b} collect?
test: The red team has {n} points, {k} points fewer than the blue team. How many points does the blue team have?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, and {b} has {k} more than that. How many {t} has {b} got?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, which is {k} fewer than {b} has. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: On a shelf in a classroom in Iowa there are {n} {t}. On the table there are {k} more {t} than on the shelf. How many {t} are on the table?
exercise: {a} skipped {n} times. {b} skipped {k} more times than {a}. How many times did {b} skip?
exercise: What number is {k} greater than {n}?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, not as many as {b}: {b} has {k} more. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} picked {k} more strawberries than {a} at a farm in Kent. {a} picked {n}. How many strawberries did {b} pick?
exercise: Count on {k} from {n}. Where do you land?
test: {n} is {k} less than which number?
test: {a}'s school collected {n} cans for a food drive, {k} fewer than {b}'s school. How many cans did {b}'s school collect?
test: How many {t} does {b} own if {b} owns {k} more than {a}, and {a} owns {n}?
test: In a spelling bee in Ottawa, the green team got {n} points. The yellow team got {k} more. How many points did the yellow team get?
test: A puppy weighs {n} kg. Its mother is {k} kg heavier. How many kilograms does the mother weigh?
test: {a} has read {n} pages of a book, {k} pages fewer than {b}. How many pages has {b} read?
exercise: {a}'s got {n} {t}, {b} got {k} more. how many {b} got
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, that's {k+1}, no wait, {k} fewer than {b}. how many {b} got
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}, {k} fewer than {b}. my mate says u take away {k} from {n}. nah that's wrong, how many has {b} got
exercise: {a} skipped {n} times, {b} skipped {k} more, it was like {n+10} degrees out. how many skips {b} do
test: {k} less than some number is {n}. what's the number then
test: red team {n+3}, sorry, {n} points, that's {k} fewer than blue. blue got how many
test: puppy's {n} kg, its mum's {k} kg heavier, and the puppy's only {k+1} weeks old. how heavy's the mum in kg
exam: It is given that {a} holds {n} {t} and that {b} holds {k} {t} in excess thereof. Determine the number of {t} held by {b}.
exam: Whereas the holding of {a}, amounting to {n} {t}, is {k} fewer than that of {b}, ascertain the holding of {b}.
exam: A shelf bears {n} {t}; a table bears {k} {t} more than the said shelf. State the number of {t} upon the table.
exam: Compute the number of {t} held by {b}, given that the holding of {a} is {n} {t} and is exceeded by that of {b} by {k}.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left her {t} to her grandchildren. {a} got {n}, and {b} got {k} more than {a}. How many {t} did {b} get?
exercise: {a}'s dad was let go from his job, and in his new one he earns {k} dollars a day less. Now he earns {n} dollars a day. How many dollars a day did he earn before?
test: {b} says {b.he}'s got {n} {t}, same as {a}. rubbish, {b.he}'s telling porkies, {b.he}'s got {k} more than that. how many has {b.he} really got
